      "body": "\r\n## Summary\r\n\r\nFlashInferMxFp4LinearKernel hardcodes backend=\"cute-dsl\" for the scaled FP4 GEMM. However, the CuTe DSL backend is only available on SM10x/11x GPUs. On SM12x GPUs, this causes the following failure:\r\n\r\n```\r\nflashinfer.utils.BackendSupportedError: mm_fp4 does not support backend\r\n'cute-dsl' with capability 120\r\n```\r\n\r\nFlashInfer's mm_fp4 already supports backend=\"auto\", which automatically dispatches to the best available backend for the current device (e.g., cute-dsl on SM10x, cudnn on SM12x, etc.). Since the library already knows which backend to select, there is no reason to hardcode a specific one.\r\n\r\nThis PR switches the GEMM backend from \"cute-dsl\" to \"auto\" and removes the manual backend selection logic.\r\n\r\n## What changed\r\n\r\n- `flashinfer_scaled_fp4_mm(backend=\"cute-dsl\")` → `backend=\"auto\"`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## Test Plan\r\n\r\n## Test Result\r\n\r\n---\r\n<details>\r\n<summary> Essential Elements of an Effective PR Description Checklist </summary>\r\n\r\n- [ ] The purpose of the PR, such as \"Fix some issue (link existing issues this PR will resolve)\".\r\n- [ ] The test plan, such as providing test command.\r\n- [ ] The test results, such as pasting the results comparison before and after, or e2e results\r\n- [ ] (Optional) The necessary documentation update, such as updating `supported_models.md` and `examples` for a new model.\r\n</details>\r\n\r\n",
      "changedFiles": 1,
      "comments": {
        "nodes": [
          {
            "author": {
              "__typename": "User",
              "login": "fede-kamel"
            },
            "body": "Tested end to end on an RTX PRO 4000 Blackwell (sm_120, driver 610.57) with nightly `0.30.1rc1.dev740`, flashinfer-python / flashinfer-cubin / flashinfer-jit-cache 0.7.0.post1 (`has_flashinfer()` and `has_flashinfer_cutedsl()` both True). Model: `nm-testing/TinyLlama-1.1B-Chat-v1.0-MXFP4`, greedy, two runs each, with the compile cache cleared between configurations.\n\n- **main:** both runs fail during compile/warmup with `flashinfer.utils.BackendSupportedError: mm_fp4 does not support backend 'cute-dsl' with capability 120`.\n- **with this PR's one-line change** (`backend=\"cute-dsl\"` → `backend=\"auto\"` in the `flashinfer_scaled_fp4_mm` call): `Using FlashInferMxFp4LinearKernel for MXFP4 GEMM`, both runs load and generate coherent text (\" Paris. The capital of France is Paris. ...\").\n\nThe activation quantize (`flashinfer_mxfp4_quantize(..., backend=\"cute-dsl\")`) is left as is in this PR and works on sm_120. Only the GEMM rejects the backend.",
            "createdAt": "2026-10-06T18:49:09Z",
            "databaseId": 6023170324,
            "updatedAt": "2026-10-06T18:49:09Z",
            "url": "https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/pull/51783#issuecomment-6023170324"
          },
          {
            "author": {
              "__typename": "User",
              "login": "waynehacking8"
            },
            "body": "Still needed on main (`153a17166e`, FlashInfer 0.7.2): on an RTX PRO 6000 Blackwell Max-Q, `--quantization mxfp4` on Qwen3-4B fails at boot with `SM12x cute-dsl requires NVFP4 with 128x4 scales`, and with this PR it serves through `FlashInferMxFp4LinearKernel`. Full GSM8K (5-shot, flexible) is 0.708 against 0.861 for BF16, close to the other W4A4 path (Humming, 0.685) and below weight-only Marlin (0.779). That gap is the format: at Qwen3-4B's dense shapes the auto-selected GEMM matches the exact FP32 product of its quantized operands to 1.7e-3 relative L2, while MXFP4 activations and weights cost about 16%.\n",
            "createdAt": "2026-10-17T16:35:40Z",
            "databaseId": 6236759761,
            "updatedAt": "2026-10-17T16:35:40Z",
            "url": "https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/pull/51783#issuecomment-6236759761"
          }
