  "issue_comments": [
    {
      "body": "Tested end to end on an RTX PRO 4000 Blackwell (sm_120, driver 610.57) with nightly `0.30.1rc1.dev740`, flashinfer-python / flashinfer-cubin / flashinfer-jit-cache 0.7.0.post1 (`has_flashinfer()` and `has_flashinfer_cutedsl()` both True). Model: `nm-testing/TinyLlama-1.1B-Chat-v1.0-MXFP4`, greedy, two runs each, with the compile cache cleared between configurations.\n\n- **main:** both runs fail during compile/warmup with `flashinfer.utils.BackendSupportedError: mm_fp4 does not support backend 'cute-dsl' with capability 120`.\n- **with this PR's one-line change** (`backend=\"cute-dsl\"` → `backend=\"auto\"` in the `flashinfer_scaled_fp4_mm` call): `Using FlashInferMxFp4LinearKernel for MXFP4 GEMM`, both runs load and generate coherent text (\" Paris. The capital of France is Paris. ...\").\n\nThe activation quantize (`flashinfer_mxfp4_quantize(..., backend=\"cute-dsl\")`) is left as is in this PR and works on sm_120. Only the GEMM rejects the backend.",
      "created_at": "2026-10-06T18:49:09Z",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/pull/51783#issuecomment-6023170324",
      "id": 6023170324,
      "updated_at": "2026-10-06T18:49:09Z",
      "user": {
        "login": "fede-kamel"
      }
    },
    {
      "body": "Still needed on main (`153a17166e`, FlashInfer 0.7.2): on an RTX PRO 6000 Blackwell Max-Q, `--quantization mxfp4` on Qwen3-4B fails at boot with `SM12x cute-dsl requires NVFP4 with 128x4 scales`, and with this PR it serves through `FlashInferMxFp4LinearKernel`. Full GSM8K (5-shot, flexible) is 0.708 against 0.861 for BF16, close to the other W4A4 path (Humming, 0.685) and below weight-only Marlin (0.779). That gap is the format: at Qwen3-4B's dense shapes the auto-selected GEMM matches the exact FP32 product of its quantized operands to 1.7e-3 relative L2, while MXFP4 activations and weights cost about 16%.\n",
      "created_at": "2026-10-17T16:35:40Z",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/pull/51783#issuecomment-6236759761",
      "id": 6236759761,
      "updated_at": "2026-10-17T16:35:40Z",
      "user": {
        "login": "waynehacking8"
      }
    }
  ],
